  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Pentland Typhoon Yagi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The strength and intensity of the typhoon Yagi left a trail of destruction, with the worst impacted regions along the coast and in mountainous regions. 299 people were killed, 34 people are missing, and 1,932 have been injured. 550 health facilities, 234,983 houses and more than 250,000 hectares of agricultural land have been damaged. Latest estimates suggest that around 1.9 million people are expected to need humanitarian assistance. Oxfam will be working with local partners to respond, with a funding need of GBP1.68M over the next 12 months. We are aiming to support 35,000 people across 15 communes of Lao Cai, Yen Bai, and Hoa Binh provinces in Northern Vietnam.</narrative>
  </description>
